    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Architecture",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#1A202C"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "9 Kaggle CSVs land in OLIST.RAW (one table per file, all VARCHAR, replayable). OLIST.STG views type, rename and deduplicate to one row per business key (one review per order, payments aggregated to the order). OLIST.MARTS is a star schema materialized as tables: DIM_DATE, DIM_CUSTOMER (grain: customer_unique_id), DIM_SELLER, DIM_PRODUCT, FCT_ORDERS (grain: order) and FCT_ORDER_ITEMS (grain: item). A Snowflake SEMANTIC VIEW (SV_ORDERS) defines the KPIs once; the DAX measures mirror it name for name.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "color": "#1A202C"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Business rules",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#1A202C"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Delivered = status 'delivered' with a customer delivery timestamp. Late = delivered after the estimated date (calendar days). Low review = score 1 or 2. Interstate = primary seller state differs from customer state. Analysis window = orders purchased Jan 2017 to Aug 2018 (edges of the dataset are sparse); applied in the Power Query partitions of both facts.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "color": "#1A202C"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Data quality checks (sql/90_checks.sql)",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#1A202C"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Unique keys in every mart; row counts RAW = STG = MARTS; GMV reconciled to the cent (R$ 13,591,643.70) across RAW, FCT_ORDERS and FCT_ORDER_ITEMS; zero orphan keys; 775 canceled/unavailable orders without items kept and documented; review duplicates resolved to the latest answer per order; geolocation averaged per zip prefix inside the Brazil bounding box.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "color": "#1A202C"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Governance",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#1A202C"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Power BI connects in Import mode with the read-only role BI_READER, which can only see OLIST.MARTS. Naming follows dbt conventions (stg_, dim_, fct_). The report is saved as a Power BI Project (PBIP: TMDL + PBIR) and versioned in Git. Comment themes come from rule-based SQL because Cortex AI functions are not enabled on trial accounts; the Cortex version is written and ready for production.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "color": "#1A202C"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Every number reconciled against the warehouse before use.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#718096"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
